The work begins with the simulation of the short rate and the numéraire, and verifies consistency with a given zero-coupon curve. From there, it proceeds through the pricing of swaps, the computation of
future Mark-to-Market (MtM) distributions, and the calculation of risk metrics such as Expected Exposure (EE),Potential Future Exposure (PFE), Credit Valuation Adjustment (CVA), and Funding Valuation Adjustment (FVA),
considering both uncollateralized and collateralized scenarios.
All analyses are performed numerically via Monte Carlo simulations, aiming to reflect realistic market conditions. Credit risk is assessed using provided Credit Default Swap (CDS) spreads, while the impact of 
collateral and funding costs is explicitly evaluated through adjustments to the transaction value.
